{"ranking": ["M2", "M4", "M1"], "fault": "M2 (bottom device of the output branch) is corrupted: its size is too small for the 20 uA branch current, so it cannot carry the current in saturation. Its drain node o is pulled down to 0.15 V, below Vdsat = 0.155 V, which pushes it into triode. This causes the output-current error, the poor compliance and the low rout. Restoring M2's width (or matching it to M1's W/L) should fix all three failing specs."}
